  <ansi fg="command">help guardian</ansi>     guardians and their guards
  <ansi fg="command">help battlescreen</ansi> the web client's battle picture
  <ansi fg="command">help evasion</ansi>      Attack and Evasion: the skill each level brings
  <ansi fg="command">help defense</ansi>      blocks, parries, and dodges
  <ansi fg="command">help shields</ansi>      shield sizes, and who may carry them
  <ansi fg="command">help armor</ansi>        armor, its bulk, and each class's training
  <ansi fg="command">help burden</ansi>       how your own load cuts your dodge
  <ansi fg="command">help interrupts</ansi>   broken chants, wind-ups, and shield counters
  <ansi fg="command">retreat [exit]</ansi>    prepare one round, then withdraw the company (or <ansi fg="command">flee</ansi>)
  <ansi fg="command">consider [enemy]</ansi>  your company's chances against a group
  <ansi fg="command">help assessment</ansi>   what scout and consider weigh
  <ansi fg="command">help coordination</ansi> how enemy groups fight together, heal, and recover
  <ansi fg="command">formation</ansi>         see and arrange your company's formation
  <ansi fg="command">company chemistry</ansi> your company's chemistry
  <ansi fg="command">help statuses</ansi>     what a critical hit leaves behind
  <ansi fg="command">help hexes</ansi>        a Witch's hexes, and how they land
  <ansi fg="command">help halberdier</ansi>   a Halberdier's sweep, brace and hook
  <ansi fg="command">heal wounds</ansi>       tend the company's wounds after a fight
  <ansi fg="command">company patch</ansi>     heal the company to its threshold (<ansi fg="command">help patch</ansi>)
  <ansi fg="command">sharpen</ansi>           sharpen your company's blades
  <ansi fg="command">help campwatch</ansi>    raiders at camp, and the watch that spots them
  <ansi fg="command">light</ansi>             how well you can see here
  <ansi fg="command">set combatpace</ansi>    how fast a round's lines come to you

In the tutorial, the Practice Yard lets you try all of this against straw
soldiers that can't hurt you (<ansi fg="command">help tutorial</ansi>).
Repeated enemy names become fixed labels such as the first cutthroat and
the second cutthroat. A survivor keeps its label when another falls; see
<ansi fg="command">help narration</ansi> for pronouns and names.

Walking into a dangerous room can spring a battle on you; its foes are set by
the zone's level band and are yours alone (<ansi fg="command">help encounters</ansi>).

Some enemies surrender or flee when their group breaks (help morale). After victory, answer each surrendered foe’s mercy question (help mercy).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Member orders</ansi>

Members fight automatically. Safe <ansi fg="command">ask [member]</ansi> orders
manage gear and provisions outside battles; conversation and observation
remain available in battle. Old queued orders recheck ownership and presence.
See <ansi fg="command">help ask</ansi> for the compatibility commands.

Group healing reaches your present company without a player party. A chant
rechecks life, presence and ownership, and healing stops at wound limits
(<ansi fg="command">help friendly-effects</ansi>).

Leaving a battle: <ansi fg="command">retreat [exit]</ansi> (or <ansi fg="command">flee</ansi>) prepares for one round,
then attempts to move the company together. See <ansi fg="command">help retreat</ansi>.

For player alliances and opt-in following/support, see <ansi fg="command">help party</ansi>.

Shared cargo and deliberate equipment assignment: <ansi fg="command">help equipment</ansi>.
Pooled gold: <ansi fg="command">help treasury</ansi>. Battle spoils: <ansi fg="command">help loot</ansi>.

Ambushes, clusters, leaping enemies, narrow ground, fatigue, and cold affect battles: help battlefield and help ambush.

Speed, personal burden and armor bulk set your turns each round: <ansi fg="command">help tempo</ansi>.

Natural health recovery pauses throughout a battle, including between blows.
Healers still heal by spells; ordinary buffs keep their real-time durations.

Strength adds bounded damage even against an equal opponent (<ansi fg="command">help strength</ansi>).
Maximum health grows only a little with level; skill decides fights (<ansi fg="command">help progression</ansi>).
Each point of a stat over your opponent's counts the same at every level (<ansi fg="command">help stat-edge</ansi>).
A promoted character fights with its class's ranks, and some summon allies (<ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help summoning</ansi>).
